Documentation was prepared so that others can understand, use, and maintain the project. The final report includes a title page, certificate, acknowledgement, abstract, introduction, literature survey comparing the existing and proposed systems, system requirements, design diagrams, implementation details with screenshots, testing results, discussion, conclusion, future scope, and references. A sample abstract reads as follows: this project presents a Smart Attendance Management System that uses face recognition to automate attendance marking, identifying students through a webcam, recording attendance in a database, and generating reports through a web dashboard, thereby reducing manual effort, preventing proxy attendance, and improving accuracy. The objectives were to automate attendance, eliminate proxy marking, provide real-time and exportable reports, and store user data securely. Future improvements include a mobile app, mask-aware recognition, cloud deployment, integration with the college ERP, and email alerts for low attendance.
